{
  "summary": "Refactors wallet fee bumping by updating CreateRateBumpTransaction to return a util::Expected containing either a BumpTransaction or BumpError struct instead of relying on out parameters. Additionally, it explicitly rejects rate bump requests when original_change_index points to an output without an extractable destination, such as an OP_RETURN, returning an INVALID_PARAMETER error.",
  "problem": "When bumping fees with original_change_index pointing to an output lacking a destination (such as an OP_RETURN data output), the wallet silently dropped that output and created a new change output instead of rejecting the call. Additionally, CreateRateBumpTransaction passed results and errors across multiple out parameters, which was cumbersome to extend with new metadata.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'The pre-existing behaviour silently replaced the specified output if an OP_RETURN output was specified.'",
    "Commit d11db9b5fb: 'Such an output, like an OP_RETURN, was silently dropped from the bumped transaction and change sent to a new address.'",
    "PR description: 'This change makes it easier for #35302 to add a sp_recipients field to the Result Struct instead of adding a new output parameter.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": [
      "#35302"
    ]
  },
  "scope_notes": "",
  "changed_since_previous": "",
  "card": "This PR refactors CreateRateBumpTransaction to return a util::Expected struct rather than multiple out parameters, and validates original_change_index to reject outputs lacking a destination (such as OP_RETURN). Previously, specifying such an index caused the wallet to silently drop the output and direct change to a fresh address. The refactor also simplifies extending the bump fee result for Silent Payments in #35302.",
